From f021646c08fa4998b85f34fdf0bda23cabb09fc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:42:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] update pause cancels a mid-tool turn after 30 s and
 keeps it resumable

A Desktop/TUI turn inside a long tool call (a foreground `sleep 600`) never reached a step
boundary, so the core-update pause could not land and the turn held the update for the whole
window (t_01a1c7cf6f171e47, part A of t_01a1c7c587142bb7).

Now a per-turn watcher (update_pause.start_mid_tool_cancel, started next to the boundary hook in
prompt_turn._invoke_agent) polls the pause request. MID_TOOL_GRACE_S = 30 s after the later of
the request's first sighting and the newest running call's start, a still-running call of an auto-continuable
turn (not_resumable_reason is None) is cancelled through agent.interrupt, the user-Stop path
(terminal foreground kill, process-group interrupt, abandoned sequential worker). The executor
persists `[interrupted by Hermes update at <UTC>Z: re-run if still needed]` as each cancelled
call's result; finished calls of a parallel step keep their real results. The next step boundary
(turn_iteration_prep.begin_iteration) consumes the cancel and runs the normal boundary pause, so
the turn ends exactly as a between-step pause (marker kept with reason core_update_pause, pause
counted, reservation released, announce_pause) and startup_resume continues it with pause_note.
The cancel never relabels a pending interrupt (a user Stop or redirect wins; interrupt_control
_REASON_UPDATE_PAUSE carve-out) and is not a user intervention; a Stop that wins keeps the call's
own result. A committed call leaves the in-flight set even when its worker was abandoned on a
timeout, so a later request cannot cut a model call. The stamp carries no subdirectory hint. A
request withdrawn before the boundary clears the cancel's own interrupt (clear_interrupt
only_reason, under the publish lock, so a Stop that landed during the hook still ends the turn)
and the turn continues; a
later request in the same turn may cancel again. Non-resumable turns are never cancelled.

Capability flag for hermes-sync's text grep: MID_TOOL_CANCEL = True.

The watcher uses _thread.start_new_thread, not threading.Thread: harnesses that run turn threads
inline patch threading.Thread, and an inline watcher hung three gateway suites for 300 s.

Proof:
- tests/tui_gateway/test_update_pause_mid_tool.py (28 tests): real AIAgent turn, real executor
  (sequential + concurrent), real SessionDB, real hook + watcher, startup_resume sweep in a
  fresh backend. GREEN 28/28. RED on main: collection ImportError (agent.update_pause_cancel,
  start_mid_tool_cancel absent); behavioural RED with the executor/boundary hooks reverted:
  the end-to-end tests fail (call runs to its own end, no stamp, no pause).
- 28 exact-anchor mutants of every added condition: all killed.
- Independent review (claude-opus-5-5) of the first head: 2 should-fix (Stop relabel race,
  stale in-flight after a timeout abandon) and 3 nits, all fixed here with tests;
  its exact-head re-review found one more (a Stop during the boundary hook was cleared) and a
  grace nit (oldest call), both fixed with tests.
- 305 affected test files (every file naming _run_prompt_submit, prompt.submit,
  _invoke_agent, tool_executor or turn_iteration_prep, incl. update_pause*, startup_resume,
  turn_marker): 4435 passed, 0 failed.
- scripts/check --only health: 0 blocking.
